From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt HLK-7688A SD debug
Date: Sun, 13 Jul 2026 23:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: core: skip SD ext reg probe for MT7628/MT7688 mtk-mmc

The SD 7.0 extension register probe (sd_read_ext_regs, new in v6.6)
issues CMD48 with a 512-byte data transfer.  The MT7628/MT7688 private
mtk-mmc DMA engine cannot complete this transfer (xfer_done timeout,
error -145 / -ETIMEDOUT), which aborts SD card enumeration before
/dev/mmcblk0 appears.

Clear SD_SCR_CMD48_SUPPORT during SCR decode so sd_read_ext_regs()
returns early via its existing check.  This exactly matches pre-6.6
kernels (e.g. 5.10 / OpenWrt 22.03) where the probe did not exist and
the SD card enumerated fine.  Only optional SD 7.0 extension features
(power management, cache, performance registers) are lost; normal block
I/O is unaffected.

Root cause 2 of the HLK-7688A 24.10 SD regression (root cause 1, the
missing AGPIO_CFG EPHY digital-mode setup, is fixed separately in the
mtk-mmc driver source).

Signed-off-by: Chris <chris@local>
---
 drivers/mmc/core/sd.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/sd.c
@@ -245,6 +245,15 @@ static int mmc_decode_scr(struct mmc_car
 	else if (scr->sda_spec3)
 		scr->cmds = UNSTUFF_BITS(resp, 32, 2);

+	/*
+	 * The SD extension register probe (CMD48) issues a 512-byte data
+	 * transfer that the MT7628/MT7688 mtk-mmc DMA engine cannot complete
+	 * (xfer_done timeout).  Clear CMD48 support so sd_read_ext_regs() bails
+	 * out via its existing check, matching pre-6.6 kernels where the probe
+	 * did not exist.  Only optional SD 7.0 extension features (power
+	 * management, cache) are lost; the card remains usable as a block device.
+	 */
+	scr->cmds &= ~SD_SCR_CMD48_SUPPORT;
 	/* SD Spec says: any SD Card shall set at least bits 0 and 2 */
 	if (!(scr->bus_widths & SD_SCR_BUS_WIDTH_1) ||
 	    !(scr->bus_widths & SD_SCR_BUS_WIDTH_4)) {
